{
  "$comment": "Result contracts for the alpaca upstream. kind=external_text: the named fields carry third-party text and are the ONLY fields sent to the injection judge (bounded by max_chars). kind=structured: API data; strings longer than max_string_len outside free_text_fields, or instruction-shaped text in a field the schema types as an id/enum/number, withhold the result deterministically. Tools absent here pass through with the audit row marked result_unjudged. error_results: an upstream isError result is prose by nature and is exempt from typed-field length checks (instruction shape still applies). rendering=json_or_table: tools that may answer with a rendered table instead of JSON; bound their text by instruction shape only.",
